/ snapshot: a run's exact state, saved to disk or a db and run later (start.md beside this goal). This goal is the
/ plan's index and its validation: each stage is a sub-goal, each comment a behaviour we want, and the step under it
/ runs the test that proves it. Tests live under this plan's folder at the path of what they test.
Start
- call Stage1
- call Stage2
- call Stage3
- call Stage4
- call Stage5

Stage1
/ a part says it takes part (ISnapshot), and saving walks the app: each part stored at its own place
/ a saved snapshot holds each part under its path from the app, and nothing the app never marked
- call /module/snapshot/save/EachPartAtItsPlace
/ a part's state saved and started in a fresh app comes back as it was: the app's mode, what a program kept on the app,
/ the app's providers
- call /module/snapshot/save/EachPartStartsAsSaved
/ an always-fresh value (Now) and a ! name are not saved
- call /module/snapshot/save/AlwaysFreshNotSaved

Stage2
/ the call stack is saved as it lives and started exactly
/ a run saved inside a sub-goal starts there: the same frames, the same current, and it goes on from the action it was at
- call /module/snapshot/resume/StartsInTheSubGoal
/ a frame's own variables come back: a call's parameters, a loop's %item%, a handler's %error%
- call /module/snapshot/resume/FramesKeepTheirVariables
/ a goal rebuilt since the save (another hash) refuses to start
- call /module/snapshot/resume/RebuiltGoalRefuses

Stage3
/ one door from text to a snapshot
/ a snapshot written to a file and read back is a snapshot: resume takes what the file read gave
- call /module/snapshot/resume/ReadFromAFile

Stage4
/ a snapshot never carries a [Sensitive] value
/ a sensitive variable is not in the saved text; a resumed run that needs it asks again
- call /module/snapshot/save/SensitiveNotSaved

Stage5
/ the proof in plang: save, write to disk, read in a fresh app, resume at the step
/ a run saved at step 3 and resumed in a fresh app goes on from step 3 with the same variables and frames
- call /module/snapshot/resume/FreshAppGoesOn
